[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Omarchy needs a few system services and permissions on FreeBSD:

1. Enable D-Bus and seatd, and let your user use the seat, graphics, and
   sound (FreeBSD 16 restricts the sound devices to the audio group):

     sysrc dbus_enable=YES seatd_enable=YES
     service dbus start; service seatd start
     pw groupmod video -m <user>
     pw groupmod audio -m <user>

2. Load the DRM driver for your GPU (see graphics/drm-kmod), e.g.:

     sysrc kld_list+=i915kms    # or amdgpu

3. Power menu actions run shutdown(8) and acpiconf(8), which are
   restricted to the operator group:

     pw groupmod operator -m <user>

4. Mount fdescfs and Linux-compatible /proc for scripts that inspect
   processes, by adding to /etc/fstab:

     fdesc   /dev/fd   fdescfs     rw   0 0
     proc    /proc     linprocfs   rw   0 0

5. Start Omarchy from the console with:

     %%PREFIX%%/libexec/omarchy/compat/uwsm start -D Hyprland hyprland.desktop

   or pick "Omarchy" in SDDM (x11/sddm, enabled with sysrc sddm_enable=YES).
   Configuration for new users is copied into your home directory the
   first time the session starts; existing files are left alone.

Wi-Fi and Bluetooth controls in the Omarchy panels need NetworkManager and
BlueZ, which are not available on FreeBSD; use wpa_supplicant(8) and
bluetooth(4) instead. Package installs and updates from the Omarchy menu use
pkg(8), and system snapshots use ZFS boot environments (bectl(8)).
EOM
}
]
